  "result": "Shell completion no longer cuts off the command line at a `#`. `tests/test_parser.py` and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass (69 passed).\n\n- **Fix:** in `split_arg_string` (`src/click/shell_completion.py`), I set `lex.commenters = \"\"`. Python's `shlex` was treating an unquoted `#` as the start of a comment and discarding the rest of the line.\n- **Tests:** I added four cases to `tests/test_parser.py::test_split_arg_string`: `cli a#b`, `cli #foo`, `cli a #b c` and `cli \"a#b\"`.\n- **Changelog:** `CHANGES.md` had no unreleased section, so I added an \"Unreleased\" heading at the top. The entry has no issue or PR link, so add those if you want them.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
